    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d129">

                <pb facs="0293" n="197" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg197"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Day to Mr. Denby.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1898-05-20"><hi rendition="#italic">May 20,
                        1898</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1588.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    dispatch, No. 2901½, of the 2d ultimo, reporting that you have made a demand on
                    the Chinese Government that immediate action must be taken by it to carry out
                    the terms agreed upon by yourself and the Tsung-li Yamên for the settlement of
                    our claims growing out of the recent riot at Chiang Pei Ting.</p>
                <p>The Department approves your action in the matter and instructs you to follow up
                    the demand on the line of previous instructions in similar cases.</p>
                <p>Respectfully, yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">William R. Day</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
